LICENSE NOT YET CHOSEN — THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT YET LICENSED FOR REUSE.

Without an explicit license, default copyright applies and no one may legally reuse
this material, which defeats the purpose of publishing it. A license must be agreed
by all co-authors before release.

Recommended, and the usual choice for this kind of artefact:

  Code  ->  MIT (permissive, one paragraph, no attribution burden on reusers)
            or Apache-2.0 if an explicit patent grant is wanted.

  Data  ->  CC-BY-4.0 (attribution required) or CC0-1.0 (public domain dedication).
            Licensed separately from the code; state the data license in README.md
            and in the repository metadata.

To finalise:
  1. Confirm the choice with all co-authors and with Karolinska Institutet's
     research data / legal office if institutional policy applies.
  2. Replace the entire contents of this file with the chosen license text
     (https://choosealicense.com supplies canonical copies).
  3. Record the data license separately in README.md.
  4. Check that the ethics approval and participant consent forms permit public
     release of the de-identified data at all — this is a prerequisite, not a
     formality, and it governs what may be shipped in data/raw/.
